  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0068_fa8f03799be1.png\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 120px;\" /></p><p>As we know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></math></p><p>Here all capacitors are connected in series.</p><p>Thus, equivalent capacitance is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>60</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, charge&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math>.</p><p>As the capacitors are connected in series, charge on each capacitor wil be same.</p>"
  }
